## Core Rules

### Always
- Read `.forge/instructions/global.instructions.md` before any code change
- Write `t.Parallel()` on every test function
- Use `t.TempDir()` for temporary file fixtures in tests
- Wrap errors: `fmt.Errorf("operation: %w", err)`
- Use `slog` for structured logging, never `fmt.Println` in production code
- Use `errcode.New(ErrXxx, ...)` for user-visible errors (see `internal/errcode`)
- Run `forge scan security` mentally before suggesting a PR

### Never
- Never add a `DROP COLUMN` to an up migration (additive-only forward migrations)
- Never swallow errors silently (`_ = err` only allowed in deferred cleanup)
- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, or credentials (environment variables only)
- Never write tests without `t.Parallel()` without an explicit comment explaining why
- Never shadow the `.gitignore` forge-managed block

### Code Generation
- Prefer table-driven tests (`[]struct{ name, input, want }`)
- Keep functions under 50 lines; extract helpers for anything longer
- One primary concern per file; `_test.go` files live alongside source
- SQL migrations: always include both `-- migrate:up` and `-- migrate:down` sections

## Forge Commands
```
forge ship <feature>     # 5-checkpoint pipeline for new features
forge scan security      # OWASP + secrets scan
forge lint               # Convention lint
forge clean --check      # Hygiene check (run before every commit)
forge doctor             # Diagnose setup issues
```

## Architecture Notes
- HTTP handlers live in `internal/handler/`
- Business logic in `internal/service/`
- Database access in `internal/store/`
- Migrations in `migrations/` (timestamped SQL files)
- Integration tests in `tests/integration/`
- Security/RLS boundary tests in `tests/security/`
